module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.RingHom.Flat
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Maps
public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.TensorProduct.Tower
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Finiteness.Defs

/-! # Annihilator of a finite module under flat base change

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Lemma Tag 07T8, second assertion for a finite module
(blueprint: lem-trf-annihilator-finite-flat-base-change).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

namespace Module

/--
Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Lemma Tag 07T8, second assertion for a finite module
(blueprint: lem-trf-annihilator-finite-flat-base-change).

For a flat map of commutative rings, the annihilator of a finitely generated module
commutes with extension of scalars. The map is represented by an algebra homomorphism,
which carries the same ring-map data together with its canonical scalar structure.
The proof chooses finitely many generators (adjoining a zero generator if necessary),
forms the simultaneous map from the ring to a finite product of copies of the module,
and tensors its kernel sequence with the flat target. The tensor identifications turn
this kernel into the ideal generated by the original annihilator. The chosen generators
also generate the base-changed module, so this kernel is its annihilator.
-/
theorem annihilator_tensorProduct_flat_base_change
    {R : Type u} {S : Type v} {M : Type w}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Algebra R S]
    (φ : R →ₐ[R] S) (hφ : φ.toRingHom.Flat)
    [Module.Finite R M] :
    Module.annihilator S (TensorProduct R S M) =
      Ideal.map φ (Module.annihilator R M) := by
  sorry

end Module
